diff --git a/docs/RemixNumosAPI.md b/docs/RemixNumosAPI.md
index b3e21e2d2..1b13a3fd1 100644
--- a/docs/RemixNumosAPI.md
+++ b/docs/RemixNumosAPI.md
@@ -52,3 +52,11 @@ fog histories across a policy change. VR uses the Standard sky policy.
 `rainbow.depthMeters` (600) describe the start and thickness of the sunlit rain in haze metres.
 The primary and secondary are centred on the antisolar direction. Ground sunlight supplies their colour.
 Cloud and near-haze visibility are sampled along the part of the curtain in front of the camera surface.
+
+## Editing a live sky
+
+In the Alt+X developer menu, Game Setup → Step 2: Parameter Tuning → Sky Tuning uses the same `rtx.skyMode` option as the API.
+Enhanced adds six tabs and a built-in weather selector. Graphics Settings exposes the night, haze and
+cloud controls. These widgets set the live option layer used by `SetConfigVariable`. A later companion
+write takes effect there too. The preset window shows the game's incoming and outgoing weather and blend.
+Recognized built-in names use the menu language. Other game identifiers are shown verbatim.
diff --git a/docs/fork-touchpoints.md b/docs/fork-touchpoints.md
index 068e0a695..f91440805 100644
--- a/docs/fork-touchpoints.md
+++ b/docs/fork-touchpoints.md
@@ -4201,3 +4201,18 @@ The ray pass binds the existing blue-noise array in `rtx_fork_numos_rays.cpp`. T
 common spectral gain and the planet tangent in both its normal and diagnostic fills. Its base variant and the
 mist and rainbow implementations keep their previous paths. `test_enhanced_sky.cpp` checks the limiting
 channel, zero radiance channels and the horizon of an elevated camera.
+
+## Translated Enhanced sky menus
+
+- `src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui.cpp`, `rtx_user_menu.cpp` and `rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp`
+  enter the Enhanced controls from the existing Sky Mode selector and Graphics Settings. The same
+  effective device mode handles VR. `dxvk_imgui_about.cpp` credits the sky author and integration contributor.
+- `rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp` and its header adapt the MIT integration's tabs and in-memory weather
+  selector. `rtx_numos_settings.*` resolves the pinned fields, and `rtx_numos_ui_fields.inl` supplies their
+  labels and help. `src/dxvk/meson.build` includes the new sources.
+- `rtx_numos.*`, `rtx_numos_ui_state.h`, `rtx_numos_policy.h` and `rtx_numos_weather.h` expose a
+  requested snapshot of resolved weather, ground height and renderer diagnostics across the two threads.
+- `rtx_option_layer.h` and `rtx_option.cpp` scope the existing user option layer to a live menu edit.
+  `rtx_gui_widgets.h` and `rtx_imgui.*` let a widget supply translated help while retaining the option
+  key, layer and reset menu. The sky unit case checks library coverage and option-layer selection.
+- `i18n/tools/update_strings.py` extracts menu text and the per-field table into the six catalogs.
diff --git a/documentation/NumosSky.md b/documentation/NumosSky.md
index c11da8dbb..250e5e012 100644
--- a/documentation/NumosSky.md
+++ b/documentation/NumosSky.md
@@ -134,3 +134,15 @@ For a library update, check the following files.
 - `numos_host.slangh`, its transitive headers in the Meson dependency list, and the resource names it expects.
 - The NUMOS section of `ThirdPartyLicenses.txt`.
 - `RtxOptions.md`, which has to be regenerated.
+
+### Remix menus
+
+Sky Tuning exposes Sky, Clouds, Haze, Night, Weather and Setup for an effective Enhanced sky. On Setup,
+All settings searches the translated names, descriptions and option keys of the 221 live library fields.
+The graphics settings window offers a shorter selection. The Weather presets window applies the library's
+eleven built-in weathers or returns to the editable Custom settings. To tune fields controlled by a game
+preset, select Custom settings and turn off Follow game weather.
+
+The present thread requests a copy of the render thread's effective weather and diagnostics while a sky
+page is open. Menu edits use deferred RTX option writes. The game can apply its weather and look again
+on a map start or a change of weather.
diff --git a/i18n/README.md b/i18n/README.md
index edba7f3cd..6b5227397 100644
--- a/i18n/README.md
+++ b/i18n/README.md
@@ -111,3 +111,12 @@ conversions. A language change rebuilds the font atlas with that language's glyp
 
 Weather preset names are localized for display, including the current/target/previous status.
 Preset keys passed to the weather system and exported to configuration files remain unchanged.
+
+### Enhanced sky labels and help
+
+`src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui_fields.inl` maps library setting suffixes to the English labels and
+tooltips shown in All settings. The four game moons share six entries and keep distinct option keys.
+`update_strings.py` extracts the text in this table and the additional labels and help in the two menu
+views. Built-in weather names in the selector are display text. The option stores the library's stable
+preset identifier. When changing a label or help, regenerate the catalogs and run the font and format
+checks above.
