+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:866
+msgid "Adds haze, fog and sun shafts to the air between you and distant terrain, buildings and clouds. It is the main sense of depth outdoors."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:870
+msgid "Haze Amount"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:871
+msgid "How much dust and haze is in the air. 1 is typical. Higher values give a hazier, whiter sky, thicker haze over distant land and a larger glow around the sun."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:875
+msgid "Scale used to measure distance through haze. 1 is real size. A smaller scale puts more haze between the camera and the same surface."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:879
+msgid "Ground Fog Visibility"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:880
+msgid "How far you can see through low-lying fog, in meters. Lower values give thicker fog: 50 is thick fog, 1000 mist and 10000 light haze. 0 turns the ground fog off."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:884
+msgid "Sun Shafts"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:885
+msgid "Lets buildings, trees and doorways shadow the haze. This gives sun shafts and keeps interiors from filling with sunlit haze. It costs some GPU time."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:888
+msgid "Light Glow in Haze"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:889
+msgid "Lets lamps, fires, muzzle flashes and other lights glow in the nearby haze. It costs more GPU time where many lights are close together on screen."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:895
+msgid "Night Brightness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:896
+msgid "Brightens the night: moonlight, starlight and the night sky, together. 0 is physically correct, which looks darker on a screen than to your eyes at night. Each step of 1 doubles the brightness. Sunlight, sunsets and your own lights are not changed."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:902
+msgid "Brightens or dims the stars and the Milky Way on top of Night Brightness, without changing the moon. Each step of 1 doubles the brightness. Daylight is not changed."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:906
+msgid "Moonlight Brightness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:907
+msgid "Brightens or dims the moon's light on the world and the sky, on top of Night Brightness. Lower it if the moon is too strong next to the stars. Daylight is not changed."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:911
+msgid "Moon Disc Brightness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:912
+msgid "Brightens or dims only the moon you see in the sky, not its light, so a blown-out moon can be tamed without darkening the night."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:918 src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui_fields.inl:71
+msgid "Draws volumetric clouds in the sky."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:920
+msgid "Cloud Coverage"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:921
+msgid "How much of the sky is covered by cloud, from 0 (clear) to 1 (overcast)."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:923
+msgid "Cloud Density"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:924
+msgid "How thick and opaque the clouds are. Higher values give darker, more solid clouds."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:927
+msgid "The kind of cloud, from 0 to 1: 0 is flat layered cloud, 0.5 broken lumpy cloud and 1 tall, puffy cumulus."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:930
+msgid "Cloud Shadows"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:931
+msgid "How strongly clouds shade the ground and the air below them, from 0 (no cloud shadows) to 1 (physical)."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:938
+msgid "Cloud Quality"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:939
+msgid "Quality draws the clouds' fine detail and sun shadows in full. Performance is faster: it uses a simpler sun shadow, so fine detail is softer and cloud tops look slightly brighter when the sun is low."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:947
+msgid "Cloud Resolution"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_numos_ui.cpp:948
+msgid "How many cloud pixels are traced each frame. The rest are rebuilt from their neighbors and earlier frames. Auto chooses from your resolution and upscaling. Full traces every pixel and costs the most. Quarter costs about a quarter and looks the same when the view is still. Sixteenth is the cheapest, but noisy and soft in motion."
+msgstr ""
+
